## T-11 — A denylisted credential is refused when NOYE_ENV = development

MUST FAIL FIRST. Cannot be executed here: `check_no_leaked_dev_fallbacks`
takes `&worker::Env`, which requires an actual Workers runtime to
construct — no `Default`, no mock constructor, and nothing in this
codebase's existing tests builds one (grep for `Env::` across
`crates/*/src` outside `env:` parameter positions returns nothing).
Recorded as `NOT RUN` for execution, per rfcs/handoffs/evidence/
README.md's rule against asserting an outcome for a command not run —
but the defect is directly readable in the shipped source, quoted
here rather than paraphrased:

crates/gateway/src/env_check.rs:82-85 (crates/core has the same shape):

    pub fn check_no_leaked_dev_fallbacks(env: &Env) -> Result<(), String> {
        if Environment::from_env(env).is_development() {
            return Ok(());
        }
        ...

With `NOYE_ENV = "development"` — which is what both shipped
`wrangler.toml` files set — this function returns `Ok(())` on its
second line, before the loop over `KNOWN_DEV_FALLBACKS` is ever
reached. It is not that the check runs and passes; it does not run at
all. This is a direct reading of the committed source, not an
inference — the early return is unconditional on `is_development()`,
with no further condition attached.

Post-fix, this becomes host-testable: Build step 3 deletes the branch
entirely, and the surviving per-variable comparison is being
refactored into a pure function (`find_leaked_fallback`) that takes
observed values directly rather than an `Env`, specifically so this
class of behavior has an automated regression test going forward. See
`rfcs/handoffs/evidence/subject-03-tests.log` for that test passing.

